questions.stem:
A tray-price helper reduces a flat fee by a per-plate charge and then takes a second discount. What prints?
class Pantry {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(100 - 10 * 2 - 20);
    }
}

A flag packer builds a shifted count in one expression. What prints?
class Packer {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int bits = 1 + 2 << 3;
        System.out.print(bits);
    }
}

A gate check prints one boolean built from four operators. What prints?
class Gate {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print(1 + 2 == 3 && 4 > 9);
    }
}

A lane-mask builder combines a number and a sum with a bitwise and. What prints?
class Masker {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int mask = 6 & 3 + 1;
        System.out.print(mask);
    }
}

A step counter adds two updates to the same variable in one expression. What prints?
class Steps {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 1;
        int total = n++ + ++n;
        System.out.print(total);
    }
}

A vane setter stores a value and also reports what it stored. What prints?
class Vane {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int v = 0;
        int r = (v = 5) + v;
        System.out.print(r);
    }
}

A gauge clamps a reading by casting it and then flipping its sign. What prints?
class Gauge {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        double d = 3.9;
        int t = -(int) d;
        System.out.print(t);
    }
}

A range check tries to write one chained comparison to test a value. What happens?
class Range {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int v = 5;
        System.out.print(1 < v < 10);
    }
}

A roster check compares a comparison with a boolean and prints one word. What prints?
class Roster {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        boolean b = 5 > 3 == true;
        String s = b ? "yes" : "no";
        System.out.print(s);
    }
}

A byte-sized counter is topped up with a compound add. What prints?
class Counter {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        byte b = 100;
        b += 50;
        System.out.print(b);
    }
}

A byte total is written with a plain assignment and the build stops. What happens?
class Total {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        byte b = 100;
        b = b + 50;
        System.out.print(b);
    }
}

A step total folds a decimal reading into an int with a compound add. What prints?
class Steps {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int k = 0;
        k += 5.9;
        System.out.print(k);
    }
}

A gauge sits one step past the top of the range a byte can hold. What prints?
class Gauge {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        byte b = 127;
        b++;
        System.out.print(b);
    }
}

A letter pointer steps forward one place with a compound add. What prints?
class Cursor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = 'a';
        c += 1;
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A balance shrinks by a computed amount using a compound subtract. What prints?
class Balance {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int x = 10;
        x -= 2 - 1;
        System.out.print(x);
    }
}

A count is folded down and then scaled with two compound steps. What integer prints? Respond with the integer only.
class Fold {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = 7;
        n %= 3;
        n *= 5;
        System.out.print(n);
    }
}

A bit reader shifts a negative count right with an unsigned compound shift. What prints?
class Bits {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        int n = -16;
        n >>>= 1;
        System.out.print(n);
    }
}

A byte total has to finish at -106 with no cast written in the source. Which statement fills the blank?
class Fold {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        byte b = 100;
        ____;
        System.out.print(b);
    }
}

A legacy badge code writes one letter with a numeric escape. What prints?
class Badge {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\101';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A sign prints two quoted words from one literal. What prints?
class Sign {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print("He said \"stop\"");
    }
}

A table check counts the characters in a two-letter label that uses a tab escape. What integer prints? Respond with the integer only.
class Table {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print("a\tb".length());
    }
}

A label tries to break a line with a unicode escape and the build stops. What happens?
class Label {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        String s = "Line\u000Abreak";
        System.out.print(s.length());
    }
}

A filename is printed with its trailing backslash protected from the compiler. What prints?
class Path {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.print("path\\n");
    }
}

A keypad code tries to name a digit with a numeric escape. What happens?
class Keypad {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        char c = '\8';
        System.out.print(c);
    }
}

A rack label pads a small number to a fixed width and ends with a bar. What prints?
class Rack {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%05d|", 42);
    }
}

A report prints a measured ratio to two decimal places. What prints?
class Report {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%.2f", 3.14159);
    }
}

A progress note prints a percent sign between two counts. What prints?
class Progress {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%d%% of %d", 3, 12);
    }
}

A split counter prints a formatted result of a whole-number division. What prints?
class Split {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%d", 7 / 2);
    }
}

A colour tag prints a byte value written in base sixteen. What prints?
class Tag {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%x", 255);
    }
}

A total is printed with an integer conversion and the run dies. What happens?
class Total {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        System.out.printf("%d", 7.0);
    }
}
